who are you under there  i'm vengeance  since his debut in detective comics all  the way back in 1939 the character of  batman has appeared in 16 different  movies  from early costume tights to feature  length live action films batman has run  the whole spectrum of genres in both  live action and animation in his film  franchises batman has turned into lego  blocks been reduced to camp and firmly  grounded in reality the newest iteration  from filmmaker matt reeves is taking  audiences all the way back to his  detective roots so without further ado  and no spoilers here is everything you  need to know before you watch the batman  over the course of the various batman  related films audiences have mostly seen  one repeated introduction to the  character generally the murder of bruce  wayne's parents followed by scenes of a  young bruce trained to become the  legendary hero while juggling his dual  identity as a rich orphan playboy and  his caped crime fighting persona the  batman does not present a young wayne  but instead presents a young batman this  film is set during the second year of  bruce wayne's exploits as a vigilante  there is a serial killer on the loose  dubbed the riddler because he leaves  riddles at each crime scene once the  riddles begin to mention the batman  specifically gotham's lieutenant jim  gordon teams up with the anonymous  masked hero in an attempt to catch the  killer before the riddler can strike  again when the riddles begin to connect  batman to his tragic past this  particular case becomes more personal  for the caped crusader the batman is  also an origin story for selena kyle who  is on her own mission to learn the truth  about her past kyle of course is given  the name of the beloved character of  catwoman  in her attempt to find answers she'll  tango with the worst of gotham's  criminal underworld including mob boss  carmine falcone and falcone's right-hand  man the penguin when selena's search for  answers leads directly to the batman the  duo both loners with an eye on revenge  find solace in one another after  realizing that for the first time in  each of their lives they discovered  someone who truly understands their pain  and desperation but batman's  entanglements with both selena and  lieutenant gordon will also test his  fortitude on no guns and no killing  before getting into some of the comic  and film references for reeves let's  shine the bat signal on reeve's amazing  cast first robert pattinson takes on the  role of bruce wayne and slips into the  suit and cow of batman though most know  patton's in from his twilight films at  the start of his career it's not his  association with playing a sullen  vampire in the past that makes pattinson  a perfect choice  since starring in the popular y.a series  pattinson has remade himself by working  with some of the most exciting indie  directors like the safety brothers for  good time rubber eggers for the  lighthouse and james gray for the lost  city of z reeves has matched that combo  with his own filmography with the panic  struck monster movie cloverfield  followed by let me in the eerie remake  of the instant vampire classic let the  right one in and the final two films in  the griddly rebooted planet of the apes  trilogy dawn of the planet of the apes  and war for the planet of the apes  joining pattinson as the franchise  mainstays are jeffrey wright as  lieutenant jim gordon planet of the apes  andy circus as wayne's butler alfred  pennyworth and zoe kravitz as selena  kyle kravitz recently told us about her  character's pull toward batman i think  she really wants to be free from her  past i think in the story you know i  think she's trying to  liberate herself  from a lot of trauma and a lot of pain  and um you know the cat woman that we  know and love who's really able to  relish and enjoy the chaos she's not  quite there yet i think she really  is struck by the connection she has with  batman because i think both of them are  people who never feel seen or connect to  anybody and i think it's a little scary  to meet someone who  affects you the way that we affect each  other other cast members include john  tuturo as carmine falcone and peter  sarsgaard plays district attorney gil  coulson the batman's villains take two  of the most outlandish 90s movie  villains and grounds them inside gotham  with more reality-based personas deep in  the criminal underworld and deep inside  a mountain of makeup is colin farrell as  the penguin farrell recently told us  about the duality of reeves grounded  vision and the fun he got to have under  the prosthetics the one thing matt  always wanted to be aware of with this  film and i think it's really really  clear when you see it as everything is  grounded everything is believable  everything is practically reachable  through your understanding as a human  being and physically as possible as well  um but the the makeup and the thing yeah  yeah yeah so that was fun paul dano will  play the riddler whose civilian identity  in the film edward nashton is one of his  known aliases in the pages of dc comics  dano's take on the riddler promises to  be far different from jim carrey's in  batman forever right from the get-go of  matt's script he had a really clear  point of view  of what he was bringing to this film  you could see the film as you read it  and  something that i was really  moved by  was  that he was exploring the two sides of  trauma maybe and you know the batman is  born of trauma right bruce wayne losing  his parents and i guess i was really  interested also in the mask and the idea  that  a vigilante in our world you know we can  see what we we often can see what we  want to see and  even though to a lot of people the  batman stands for good i can tell you  that i as my character  saw him representing exactly what i  wanted to as a as a great source of  inspiration and and power  the riddler serial killer is where  reeves was able to pull in the  influences that would return the batman  to his detective routes from 2020's  first trailer unveiling at dc fandom  through every bit of press now reeves  has emphasized repeatedly that batman is  not an origin film to start in batman's  second year reeves mined numerous  sources both within dc comics extensive  library but also some of the best  psychological thrillers and crime opuses  in film and television let's start with  dc reeves cites the long halloween by  jeff loeb and tim sale as a prominent  influence for the story set after the  events of frank miller's seminal batman  year one storyline the long halloween  sees batman attempting to learn the  identity of a serial killer this text  also accomplishes a few other things  like chronicling the continuing  deterioration of gotham's organized  crime families but the key to the long  halloween was batman encountering a  mystery he could not easily crack early  on reeves said he wanted to emphasize  batman as the world's greatest detective  an element of the character generally  downplayed in the more action-oriented  film cycles made by zack snyder and  christopher nolan while also playing up  the noirish elements inherent in the  concept at a recent q a reeves said from  long halloween i was thinking about the  calendar man and the different sort of  killings and then this idea came to me i  thought we could do a thing where at  these crimes there's correspondence left  for the batman so the idea that suddenly  someone is shining a light on him and  that would be very unsettling to him  reeves continued at the qa by saying i  thought about the zodiac killer and i  thought about how in this horrific way  the zodiac left all these ciphers and  these communications to the police and  to the newspaper and how unsettling that  was  and i thought wow that actually sounds  like a horrifying version of the riddler  because he leaves all these puzzles  while reeves has brought up zodiac fans  online have picked up on another david  fincher vibe for the riddler noticing a  similar visual palette to his earlier  fictional serial killer film seven but  this should not suggest that the batman  is a straight adaptation of the long  halloween as beyond subbing in the  riddler as the serial murderer someone  key to the story is missing from the  film harvey dent who would become  two-face  in lieu of harvey peter sarsgaard plays  the corrupt district attorney gil  coulson an original character for the  film jamie lawson also plays an original  character in the film bella rial who is  running for mayor and challenges bruce  wayne to do more good deeds for the  citizens of gotham yep it looks like  robert pattinson is in another franchise  with a fearless woman named bella  for pattinson however instead of the  long halloween reeve suggested that the  actor read darwin cook's ego which  details bruce wayne's grappling with  batman's moral code and whether he wants  to continue crime fighting pattinson  told us how he wrestled with that idea  what i got from ego  and from quite a few other comics is  he he believes it he when he believes  and he puts on the suit he disappears  and i thought it was interesting to kind  of think that  bruce feels  as himself  impotent to help anybody and  [Music]  and avenge his parents he needs to  completely embrace his alter ego and so  in our telling of the story like bruce  hasn't really got control of his persona  as bruce yet like he's just  he's a recluse that can he's a recluse  and he's not he's not the kind of  playboy that we've seen in other tongues  of the story like he's  he's a freak nevertheless the batman  takes the thematic ideas from the long  halloween and batman ego and leaves most  of their plots within its pages beyond  finchers zodiac and fincher's fbi series  mine hunter reeves has also cited the  award-winning detective dramas the  french connection in chinatown as  neo-noir influences on the batman but  let's not get too far removed from the  batman we know and love sure there's a  serial killer a cat burglar and gotham  politicians and gangsters but there's  also the batmobile forgetting the more  outlandish design conventions  established in batman 89 this car is in  fact a muscle car with some obvious  modifications long time readers of the  batman comics may even recognize the  broad strokes of the design as the one  batman used throughout most of the 1980s  and into the 90s  despite all the telltale markings of a  reboot the batman's place in the loose  continuity of dc film slate is still up  for debate during the early phase of  development reeves suggested it could  take place outside of continuity like  todd phillips's joker but quickly  backpedaled to say it will likely have  some ties to the known dc universe and  that there may even be a cameo or two  but then again the dc universe is a  place where world changing events can  create convenient retcons  there will be multiple previous batman  chiefly michael keaton and ben affleck  in the flash for example as for now this  specific batman is in his own specific  gotham what we do know is that pattinson  and reeves have discussed a trilogy  i've talked to matt about the idea of  doing a trilogy and uh  and that would be wonderful i mean i  really really enjoyed the process and  it's such a fun character to play and  yeah it'll be that'd be lovely the  batman will be released at the beginning  of a full 2022 roster for the dc film  universe which includes the flash  aquaman and the lost kingdom and black  adam we wouldn't put it past warner  brothers to try and eventually connect  them to the batman but we won't be  disappointed if they remain separate in  the meantime though the principal cast  is expected to return for at least two  sequels to the batman so strap in for  175 minutes and try to decipher all the  clues in the batman for where reeves and  perhaps dc might be going from march  through the rest of the year for today  now you know everything you need to know  before you watch the batman  [Music]  you

